1
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:33,960
Want to take a walk with me?

2
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:20,000
...continue to protest the presence
of a convicted sex offender

3
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:22,400
in their neighborhood.
Michelle Betler reports.

4
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:25,040
Thanks, Rick. I'm standing here
on Woodward Court,

5
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:26,680
the quiet residential
street

6
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:28,800
that has become
the focus of controversy

7
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:31,920
ever since 48-year-old
Ronald James McGorvey returned here

8
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:33,680
after serving a two-year
prison sentence

9
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:35,680
for indecent exposure
to a minor.

10
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:37,640
In the past few days
an organization

11
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:39,720
known as the Committee
of Concerned Parents

12
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:42,760
began distributing these notices
throughout the community

13
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:44,960
warning neighbors
of what they call a quote,

14
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,920
"Dangerous predator
in our midst."

15
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:50,280
I don't really like having
him that close to my family.

16
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:53,800
I think it's outrageous.
This block has too many children

17
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:56,720
for a sex offender to, uh, be
moving in the neighborhood.

18
00:01:56,760 --> 00:01:58,520
I-- I don't think
it's a good idea.

19
00:01:58,560 --> 00:02:00,880
Makes me very nervous.
Makes me a little enraged.

20
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:03,800
Um, I'd have a problem
if I see him on the street.

21
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:06,000
It's like having an
alcoholic work in a bar.

22
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,279
They don't mix.
They shouldn't be together.

23
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:11,360
The conditions of his parole
expressly forbid McGorvey

24
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:13,440
to be within 100 yards
of any playground,

25
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:16,960
school or recreation area
where children normally gather.

26
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:18,920
These conditions seem
to be of little comfort

27
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:21,480
to the many parents whose
children play and go to school

28
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:23,280
in this formerly
tranquil community,

29
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:26,560
and who in the coming days and weeks
will be hoping for the best

30
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:29,320
but preparing for the worst.
Rick, back to you.

31
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:42,600
My husband and I had an
actual spiritual experience.

32
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:45,720
We did this intense
spa treatment--

33
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,360
- Oh, come on.
- No, listen to me.

34
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:50,640
It was on our vacation in Cabo
and there were eight other couples

35
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:52,720
and this Mayan woman.

36
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:54,760
A goddess,
just a goddess.

37
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:56,200
- She had--
- She's due in September.

38
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:58,680
She thinks she's gonna
take three months off,

39
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:01,240
then it's Christmas, then she'll be back
to work the first of the year.

40
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:02,760
Please.

41
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:05,680
Six months from now she'll be right here
on this bench with us.

42
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:07,520
My friend Beth said
that the way she did it

43
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:10,760
was to just take him with her every time
she went to the bathroom.

44
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:13,720
- I find that strange.
- Yeah, that's what I said to Beth.

45
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:15,120
It's Oedipal.

46
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:17,040
What's the rush?

47
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:20,040
Although I will say, when I was trying
to potty-train Christian,

48
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:22,760
I opened the diaper
and it was huge!

49
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:24,480
Like a grown man.

50
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:28,000
Smiling politely to mask a
familiar feeling of desperation

51
00:03:28,040 --> 00:03:31,760
Sarah reminded herself to think
like an anthropologist.

52
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:35,680
She was a researcher studying the
behavior of typical suburban women.

53
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:37,200
They weren't organic?

54
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:40,120
She was not a typical
suburban woman herself.

55
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:42,320
Troy, stop that!

56
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:43,760
Paul and I were having
sex the other night

57
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:45,800
and I drifted off
right in the middle of it.

58
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:47,600
It happens.

59
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:50,640
Yeah, I guess.
But when I woke up and apologized

60
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:52,440
he said he hadn't
even noticed.

61
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:54,160
You know what
you should do?

62
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:56,720
Set aside a specific
block of time for it.

63
00:03:56,760 --> 00:03:59,440
That's what Louis and I do--
every Tuesday night at 9:00.

64
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:01,440
"Whether you want to or not"
Sarah thought,

65
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:03,760
her eyes straying over
to the play area.

66
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:07,880
Even at such a tiny
playground as this

67
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:10,960
Lucy didn't interact much
with the other children.

68
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,400
Sarah didn't really know why
they even bothered coming here,

69
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:15,400
except that she'd
probably go crazy

70
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:17,120
trapped in the house
all day

71
00:04:17,159 --> 00:04:19,240
with this unknowable
little person.

72
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:27,920
Morning snack time
was 10:30 on the dot...

73
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:30,080
Snack time!

74
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:32,680
...a regimen established
and maintained by Mary Ann,

75
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:35,280
who believed that rigid
adherence to a timetable

76
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:37,160
was not only the key
to a healthy marriage,

77
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:39,160
but to effective
parenting as well.

78
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:41,680
- I'll take this one!
- I want that one!

79
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:46,840
- Can I do it?
- Yeah. Ready?

80
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:52,200
Mommy...

81
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:54,120
where's my snack?

82
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:56,440
I'm sorry, honey,
Mommy can't find it.

83
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:58,640
- I forgot the rice cakes.
- Poor thing.

84
00:04:58,680 --> 00:05:00,680
- I'm sure it's in here somewhere.
- Second time this week.

85
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:02,520
Well, who's going to keep
track of everything?

86
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:04,720
- Bad mommy. Bad mommy.
- Just calm down, please.

87
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:08,400
No calm down!
I want my snack!

88
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:10,680
All right, you know what?
It's--

89
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:13,480
it's just not here, okay?
See for yourself.

90
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:18,320
Wait!

91
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:21,160
Troy, honey,
give Lucy your goldfish.

92
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:22,880
No!

93
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:24,600
Troy Jonathan,
give me those goldfish!

94
00:05:24,640 --> 00:05:26,040
But, Mama, they're mine.

95
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:28,520
No back talk.
You can share with your sister.

96
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:30,680
Troy has goldfish for you.
Go sit down.

97
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:32,760
That's much more than 10.

98
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:35,160
- That's great.
- Look how big I made my lawn.

99
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:37,600
Thank you, Mary Ann,
you're a life saver.

100
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:40,840
It's nothing.
I just hate to see her suffer like that.

101
00:05:42,440 --> 00:05:44,880
Maybe you should make
a checklist and tape it to the door

102
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:47,320
so it's the last thing you
see before leaving the house.

103
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:49,400
That's what I do.

104
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:53,040
Yeah, thank you. That's-- that's
a really helpful suggestion.

105
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:56,080
You're welcome.

106
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:58,240
Drink your juice.

107
00:05:58,280 --> 00:06:00,040
Are you the plane again?

108
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:01,320
Look.

109
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:03,720
Now you have to act like me.

110
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:06,040
The prom king.

111
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:09,480
Oh my God,
he's back.

112
00:06:09,520 --> 00:06:11,280
Sarah followed
the other women's gazes

113
00:06:11,280 --> 00:06:12,640
over to the entrance
of the playground,

114
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:15,760
eager to finally get a glimpse
of the prom king,

115
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:18,240
the handsome and mysterious
young father

116
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:20,400
who had been a regular
at the Walker Street playground

117
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:22,960
for several weeks
this past spring

118
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,960
before abruptly
dropping out of sight.

119
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:29,560
I don't need a rest.
I need an airplane ride.

120
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:32,520
His departure had left a gaping
hole in the emotional lives

121
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:34,880
of Cheryl, Theresa
and Mary Ann.

122
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:37,880
Barely a day went by without one
of them speculating wistfully

123
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:41,320
about the reason for his absence
and the likelihood of his return.

124
00:06:43,200 --> 00:06:47,280
Here I come.
There's no room for two of us, diesel.

125
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:49,640
You've done it again.

126
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:51,240
I hate steam engines.

127
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:54,080
When I come back I will
pinch you with my pinchers.

128
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:57,520
Yeah?
Well, when I come back

129
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:59,200
I'm gonna ram you
with my rammer.

130
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:01,040
- Ready?
- No, you won't.

131
00:07:03,440 --> 00:07:07,720
Every time you win,
diesel!

132
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:10,520
I know.

133
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:13,160
- Hello!
- Mommy's home.

134
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:16,000
The jester's cap was something
that truly disturbed Brad.

135
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:19,200
All day long the boy ate,
played and napped in it.

136
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:23,080
But the moment his mother stepped in
the house he had no more use for it.

137
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:25,400
As if the entire day
up to that point

138
00:07:25,440 --> 00:07:28,240
had been a pointless
and somewhat useless charade.

139
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:30,320
You got some sun
today, didn't you?

140
00:07:30,360 --> 00:07:33,000
Did Daddy forget
the sunscreen again?

141
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:37,320
What are you doing?

142
00:07:37,360 --> 00:07:40,680
That's his full name.
What's your favorite thing about him?

143
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:43,080
Um...

144
00:07:43,120 --> 00:07:45,400
I like to come over
to his house.

145
00:07:45,440 --> 00:07:46,800
Hmm.

146
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:53,000
I think I'm gonna finally break down
and get a cellphone.

147
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:55,120
- Really?
- Mmm.

148
00:07:55,160 --> 00:07:56,560
Why?

149
00:07:59,760 --> 00:08:01,800
I have no way of reaching you
when I'm out with Aaron.

150
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:03,120
You're done,
right?

151
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:07,280
You've got one.

152
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:09,200
Don't you think it's
strange that I don't?

153
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:12,920
Yeah, I do.
You just never wanted one before.

154
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:15,160
Yeah, I know.

155
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:18,600
There's a family plan.
We can talk for free.

156
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:22,160
Okay.

157
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:24,680
Let's just see where we are
at the end of the month.

158
00:08:24,720 --> 00:08:26,280
Yeah?

159
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:29,360
Are your hands okay?

160
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:46,200
As was her custom each week
night after dinner,

161
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:49,400
the boy's mother sent Brad
down to the municipal library

162
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:52,400
to study for the bar exam.

163
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:55,640
But he never quite made it through
the door of the building.

164
00:08:58,320 --> 00:09:01,640
Brad had been watching
the skateboarders for weeks now,

165
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:04,120
sometimes for as long
as an hour at a stretch.

166
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:07,200
But he never received the slightest
acknowledgement from any of them.

167
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:12,520
He'd been the same age as these
boys when his mother died.

168
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:14,600
- You do that!
- No way!

169
00:09:14,640 --> 00:09:16,640
- Nice.
- Hey, that was nice, dude!

170
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:19,320
"I must have been like this,"
Brad sometimes thought.

171
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:23,400
"I must have been
one of them."

172
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:28,080
Awful.

173
00:09:29,880 --> 00:09:32,160
He should be castrated.

174
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:33,840
Quick and clean,
just chop it off.

175
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:36,080
Then you wouldn't have to worry
about notifying the neighbors.

176
00:09:36,080 --> 00:09:37,880
You know what else
you should do?

177
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:40,840
Nail his penis above the entrance
to the elementary school.

178
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:43,480
You know, as a warning
to other perverts.

179
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:45,240
You think
this is funny?

180
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:48,680
I just can't believe you want to
castrate a man for indecent exposure.

181
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:51,440
My brother used
to expose himself when--

182
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:53,840
when we were teenagers.
He'd do it in my bedroom,

183
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:56,320
he'd do it in the dining room,
he'd do it in the back seat of a car.

184
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:59,640
He'd always figure out a way to do it so
that nobody could see him except me.

185
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:01,800
Didn't you
tell anyone?

186
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:03,720
No, I didn't want
to get him in trouble.

187
00:10:03,760 --> 00:10:05,560
Maybe he should
be castrated.

188
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:10,080
It's not the same thing.
He wasn't doing it to strangers.

189
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:12,760
Oh my God, there he is.

190
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:15,320
After all this time,
two days in a row.

191
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:16,800
Where's the fire?

192
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:19,400
Maybe he needed a vacation.

193
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:21,760
From what?

194
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:23,880
From being
the prom king.

195
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:26,200
It's a dirty job,
but someone's gotta do it.

196
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:31,840
- Close it?
- Close it.

197
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:35,000
Close the gate.
There you go.

198
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:37,480
- It's open.
- It's all right.

199
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:40,520
- Somebody else will close it.
- Are we practicing?

200
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:45,280
Are we playing
up on the swings?

201
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:47,280
Swing time!

202
00:10:52,040 --> 00:10:53,800
What's he do for a living?

203
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:57,400
We've never actually
spoken to him.

204
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:58,760
Really?

205
00:10:58,800 --> 00:11:01,080
We don't even
know his name.

206
00:11:01,120 --> 00:11:04,120
I thought you guys said
he was a regular here.

207
00:11:04,160 --> 00:11:06,320
- It was awkward.
- He made us nervous.

208
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:09,400
You had to think about what you
were gonna wear in the morning.

209
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:12,000
You know, put on makeup.
It was exhausting.

210
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:23,160
Mommy, push me!

211
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:26,720
Okay.
I'll be right there.

212
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:33,000
Wait!

213
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:35,160
Five bucks if you get
his phone number.

214
00:11:41,680 --> 00:11:44,080
How old is she?

215
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:45,560
Lucy,

216
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:48,360
tell the nice boy
how old you are.

217
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:50,720
I'm three.

218
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:52,960
My grandma
lives in New Jersey.

219
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,920
She doesn't have
a swim pool.

220
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:57,480
Do you like to swim?

221
00:11:57,520 --> 00:12:00,720
I don't like sharks.
They eat you up.

222
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:02,640
Don't listen to him.

223
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:05,920
We go to the town pool
almost every day.

224
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:09,360
- I'm Brad, by the way.
- Sarah.

225
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:11,640
You guys come
here a lot?

226
00:12:11,680 --> 00:12:14,200
No, just the last
few weeks.

227
00:12:14,240 --> 00:12:16,400
I usually go to the one
over on Harris,

228
00:12:16,400 --> 00:12:18,640
with the big wood things,
you know, and the slide across.

229
00:12:18,640 --> 00:12:20,280
Yeah, we actually rent a house
right around the corner

230
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:21,720
from there on Ashforth.

231
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:24,640
That ice cream truck never leaves.
Such a nightmare.

232
00:12:24,680 --> 00:12:28,200
Yeah, tell me about it.

233
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:30,880
You know, you're the first person
here who's ever talked to me.

234
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:35,800
You make 'em nervous.

235
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:38,320
Oh, right.

236
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:41,560
I guess they don't see too many fathers
here during the weekdays.

237
00:12:44,840 --> 00:12:46,880
You don't have to be polite.
Go ahead and ask.

238
00:12:46,920 --> 00:12:48,720
What?

239
00:12:48,720 --> 00:12:51,800
You know, what the person who wears the
pants in the family does for a living.

240
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:55,080
Oh. All right,
what does your wife do?

241
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:58,400
- She makes documentaries.
- Oh, wow.

242
00:12:58,440 --> 00:13:01,200
- Like Michael Moore?
- Uh, like PBS.

243
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:03,720
Oh.

244
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:05,720
Well, I think it's
admirable you're here.

245
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:08,480
There's no reason fathers
can't be primary caregivers.

246
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:12,560
I finished law school
two years ago,

247
00:13:12,560 --> 00:13:15,920
but I can't seem to pass the bar exam.
Failed it twice now.

