00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:18,480
You're ready to roll?

501
00:26:18,520 --> 00:26:20,400
Could you wait
a few minutes?

502
00:26:20,400 --> 00:26:22,760
I'm sorry, Richard's barricaded
in the upstairs office

503
00:26:22,800 --> 00:26:25,560
- finishing some stuff for work.
- No problem.

504
00:26:25,600 --> 00:26:27,640
I've got a little surprise
for someone anyway.

505
00:26:27,680 --> 00:26:30,000
She's a terror at night.
I couldn't get her to nap again.

506
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:32,960
- Oh, the poor thing.
- Poor mom is more like it.

507
00:26:33,000 --> 00:26:34,960
Hello.

508
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:37,840
Is there a cute little
girl in the house?

509
00:26:37,840 --> 00:26:40,360
Oh, my goodness!

510
00:26:40,400 --> 00:26:43,080
What--

511
00:26:43,120 --> 00:26:45,440
what have I found?

512
00:26:45,480 --> 00:26:48,000
- A beanie.
- Oh, a beanie.

513
00:26:48,040 --> 00:26:49,480
Jean, you didn't
need to to that.

514
00:26:49,520 --> 00:26:53,200
Oh, this little dog needed
a girl to take care of him.

515
00:26:53,240 --> 00:26:55,920
And I know a little girl
who needed a dog.

516
00:26:57,960 --> 00:26:59,840
Let me see.

517
00:26:59,880 --> 00:27:01,520
Sarah was beginning
to get angry.

518
00:27:01,560 --> 00:27:04,040
Her evening fitness walk
was the one thing

519
00:27:04,080 --> 00:27:07,160
she looked forward to all day,
and Richard knew this.

520
00:27:09,880 --> 00:27:12,040
But if there was one thing
life had taught Richard,

521
00:27:12,080 --> 00:27:13,920
it was that it was
ridiculous

522
00:27:13,960 --> 00:27:16,960
to be at war
with your own desires.

523
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:20,440
He could easily imagine what people
would say if they could see him now--

524
00:27:20,480 --> 00:27:23,280
Exactly the same thing they'd
say if someone had told them

525
00:27:23,280 --> 00:27:26,720
that Ray from next door
was a transvestite,

526
00:27:26,760 --> 00:27:28,480
or that Ted from work

527
00:27:28,520 --> 00:27:31,080
had anonymous gay sex
at highway rest stops.

528
00:27:31,120 --> 00:27:34,320
"But we want what we want,"
Richard thought,

529
00:27:34,320 --> 00:27:36,320
"and there's not much
we can do about it."

530
00:27:37,960 --> 00:27:40,640
He had stumbled
on the site 11 months ago

531
00:27:40,680 --> 00:27:43,480
while doing research
for a consulting firm.

532
00:27:43,520 --> 00:27:46,080
His office door
was wide open.

533
00:27:46,120 --> 00:27:48,120
But he clicked
on the link anyway.

534
00:27:55,920 --> 00:27:58,000
He was deeply engrossed
in his discovery

535
00:27:58,040 --> 00:28:00,480
when Ted knocked
on his door.

536
00:28:00,520 --> 00:28:02,240
I'm taking lunch orders.
You want something?

537
00:28:02,280 --> 00:28:04,160
Casually, but with great haste

538
00:28:04,200 --> 00:28:07,080
Richard banished Slutty Kay
from his screen...

539
00:28:07,120 --> 00:28:09,240
Uh, yeah, I'll have
a chicken Caesar.

540
00:28:09,280 --> 00:28:12,560
...and reentered the flow
of an ordinary day.

541
00:28:14,840 --> 00:28:17,200
It wasn't until
several months later

542
00:28:17,240 --> 00:28:20,480
that Richard gave the slightest thought
to the site he had stumbled upon.

543
00:28:23,120 --> 00:28:24,880
Do you need me
for anything else?

544
00:28:24,920 --> 00:28:26,800
Uh, no no, you
can head home.

545
00:28:26,840 --> 00:28:28,440
I'm just gonna catch up
on some e-mail.

546
00:28:28,480 --> 00:28:31,400
Well, don't stay too late.
Your dinner will get cold.

547
00:28:39,240 --> 00:28:43,280
Lately Slutty Kay
had become a problem.

548
00:28:43,280 --> 00:28:45,240
He thought about her
far too often,

549
00:28:45,280 --> 00:28:46,560
and spent hours studying

550
00:28:46,600 --> 00:28:49,560
the thousands of photographs
available to him.

551
00:28:49,600 --> 00:28:52,360
Some of Kay's practices
struck him as bizarre,

552
00:28:52,400 --> 00:28:54,240
even off-putting.

553
00:28:54,280 --> 00:28:57,640
She had a thing
about kitchen utensils,

554
00:28:57,680 --> 00:28:59,920
spatulas, and dressing up
like a little girl

555
00:28:59,920 --> 00:29:01,560
and playing with balloons.

556
00:29:01,600 --> 00:29:04,400
But who was
Richard to judge?

557
00:29:07,520 --> 00:29:09,480
Oh, that's it.

558
00:29:09,520 --> 00:29:13,120
Though as close as Richard
sometimes felt to Slutty Kay,

559
00:29:13,160 --> 00:29:15,320
as much as he believed
that he knew her,

560
00:29:15,360 --> 00:29:17,960
he could never get past
the uncomfortable fact

561
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:22,000
that she existed for him
solely as a digital image.

562
00:29:31,600 --> 00:29:34,000
The panties were an attempt
to solve this problem.

563
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:37,880
Maybe a sniff or two
would hurry things along,

564
00:29:37,920 --> 00:29:40,400
so he could get back
downstairs to his real life,

565
00:29:40,440 --> 00:29:42,360
where his wife
was waiting for him

566
00:29:42,400 --> 00:29:45,480
her impatience increasing
by the minute.

567
00:29:45,520 --> 00:29:48,360
What are you doing?

568
00:30:39,040 --> 00:30:42,880
Are you almost finished there? 'Cause
I'd really like to go for my walk?

569
00:30:44,520 --> 00:30:47,720
- You could have knocked.
- I did!

570
00:30:49,160 --> 00:30:51,800
We need to talk.

571
00:31:02,160 --> 00:31:04,040
You're awfully quiet
this evening.

572
00:31:04,080 --> 00:31:07,240
- Everything okay?
- What?

573
00:31:07,280 --> 00:31:09,480
Yeah.

574
00:31:09,520 --> 00:31:11,560
You'll have to walk
without me tomorrow night.

575
00:31:11,600 --> 00:31:13,960
I've got a book
group meeting.

576
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:15,920
Okay.

577
00:31:15,960 --> 00:31:18,160
You're sure everything's
all right?

578
00:31:19,160 --> 00:31:21,840
Yeah, sorry.

579
00:31:21,880 --> 00:31:25,200
I guess I'm just
a little tired.

580
00:31:25,240 --> 00:31:26,920
So what are
you reading?

581
00:31:26,960 --> 00:31:28,720
"Crime and
Punishment."

582
00:31:28,720 --> 00:31:31,840
Wow. That's pretty
highbrow for a book group.

583
00:31:31,880 --> 00:31:35,440
Well, we have some
very stimulating discussions.

584
00:31:35,480 --> 00:31:37,960
You should come next month.
We're doing "Madame Bovary."

585
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:40,040
You could be
my little sister.

586
00:31:40,080 --> 00:31:41,600
Little sister?

587
00:31:41,640 --> 00:31:45,160
We're trying to get younger
women involved.

588
00:31:45,200 --> 00:31:46,960
We call them
our little sisters.

589
00:31:48,400 --> 00:31:50,720
I don't know, Jean.

590
00:31:50,760 --> 00:31:53,240
I read "Madame Bovary"
in grad school.

591
00:31:53,280 --> 00:31:55,680
It's a pretty
misogynist text.

592
00:31:55,720 --> 00:31:58,720
Well, that's an
interesting perspective.

593
00:31:58,760 --> 00:32:01,440
- You should come.
- Let me think about it.

594
00:32:01,480 --> 00:32:04,360
Oh, would you
excuse me, Jean?

595
00:32:04,400 --> 00:32:07,680
Someone's at my door.
I'll call you, okay?

596
00:32:07,720 --> 00:32:09,520
Hi!

597
00:32:12,800 --> 00:32:14,320
Hi!

598
00:32:17,640 --> 00:32:20,200
Wow, God,

599
00:32:20,240 --> 00:32:21,680
this is a surprise.

600
00:32:21,680 --> 00:32:23,640
I haven't seen
you since--

601
00:32:23,680 --> 00:32:26,120
I-- I hope you don't mind. Your husband
said you'd be back any minute.

602
00:32:26,160 --> 00:32:27,720
Oh, no,
not at all.

603
00:32:27,760 --> 00:32:30,000
It's good
to see you.

604
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:33,680
God, um, can I get you
some tea or something?

605
00:32:33,680 --> 00:32:36,040
I can only stay a minute.
I just came to warn you.

606
00:32:36,080 --> 00:32:38,600
- You know that guy, the pervert?
- Uh-huh.

607
00:32:38,640 --> 00:32:40,160
He's been riding his
bike near the playground

608
00:32:40,200 --> 00:32:42,600
- checking out the kids.
- Oh, God.

609
00:32:42,640 --> 00:32:45,200
Oh, God,
do the police know?

610
00:32:45,240 --> 00:32:47,160
Nothing they can do.
He's not breaking any laws.

611
00:32:47,200 --> 00:32:50,440
I guess they're just waiting
for him to kill someone.

612
00:32:50,480 --> 00:32:52,640
I just thought
you should know.

613
00:32:52,680 --> 00:32:56,120
Thanks, that's
nice of you.

614
00:32:56,160 --> 00:32:58,360
Let me get
you some tea.

615
00:32:58,400 --> 00:33:01,960
I'm sorry.
I-- I don't think it's a good idea.

616
00:33:04,400 --> 00:33:06,640
I didn't mean
to kiss him.

617
00:33:06,640 --> 00:33:09,760
I don't even know
how it happened.

618
00:33:13,200 --> 00:33:16,080
I'd better go.
Mike's gonna worry.

619
00:33:21,400 --> 00:33:23,720
You wanna talk?

620
00:33:23,760 --> 00:33:25,520
I'm tired.

621
00:34:55,360 --> 00:34:57,680
Hello.

622
00:34:57,720 --> 00:35:00,040
Hey.

623
00:35:00,080 --> 00:35:03,560
No, he's still
sleeping.

624
00:35:03,600 --> 00:35:06,680
Yeah, I'm, uh, I'm going
through it right now.

625
00:35:09,800 --> 00:35:13,160
No, I guess I
don't need them.

626
00:35:16,360 --> 00:35:17,640
Okay.

627
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:22,160
All right, bye.

628
00:36:23,520 --> 00:36:24,840
H-hi.

629
00:36:24,880 --> 00:36:27,080
H-hello?

630
00:36:27,120 --> 00:36:30,240
Yes, I'd like
to place an order.

631
00:36:30,280 --> 00:36:33,480
Pierce, Sarah,
Mrs.

632
00:36:35,440 --> 00:36:36,520
Um...

633
00:36:36,560 --> 00:36:40,680
it's the red bathing suit
on page 29.

634
00:36:40,720 --> 00:36:42,880
The hide-your-tummy
halter neck.

635
00:36:44,840 --> 00:36:47,320
Uh, I'm size...

636
00:36:49,680 --> 00:36:53,320
10, eight?
I mean, I think.

637
00:36:53,360 --> 00:36:55,360
E-eight.

638
00:37:35,640 --> 00:37:37,280
You want to go
in the pool?

639
00:37:37,320 --> 00:37:38,880
You do?

640
00:37:41,840 --> 00:37:45,080
One, two.

641
00:37:50,720 --> 00:37:53,600
Daddy, can I go
in the pool now?

642
00:37:53,640 --> 00:37:55,480
In a minute, okay?

643
00:37:55,520 --> 00:37:58,560
Okay.

644
00:37:58,600 --> 00:38:01,360
There you go.

645
00:38:08,360 --> 00:38:10,800
Mommy, I have
to go pee-pee.

646
00:38:10,840 --> 00:38:13,040
Just go in the pool.

647
00:38:13,080 --> 00:38:16,360
Huh-uh, I want
to go to the bathroom.

648
00:38:16,400 --> 00:38:18,240
Really?

649
00:38:18,280 --> 00:38:20,080
Okay, come on.

650
00:38:24,560 --> 00:38:26,120
Okay, ready?

651
00:38:26,160 --> 00:38:28,200
There.

652
00:38:55,960 --> 00:38:58,000
Swing down.

653
00:39:00,880 --> 00:39:03,760
Hey, I'm drumming it.

654
00:39:03,800 --> 00:39:05,000
Oh.

655
00:39:05,960 --> 00:39:08,800
Wow.

656
00:39:08,840 --> 00:39:11,280
- It's you.
- Yeah, hey.

657
00:39:11,320 --> 00:39:13,960
- Hi!
- Okay.

658
00:39:15,320 --> 00:39:17,680
I hope you don't mind.
Lucy has sensitive skin.

659
00:39:17,720 --> 00:39:20,280
She's better off
in the shade.

660
00:39:20,320 --> 00:39:22,920
Oh no,
not at all.

661
00:39:22,960 --> 00:39:24,160
It's nice
to see you again.

662
00:39:24,200 --> 00:39:26,120
Yeah, you too.

663
00:39:28,640 --> 00:39:30,960
I'm sorry,
would you get my back?

664
00:39:31,000 --> 00:39:34,000
Um...
okay, sure.

665
00:39:34,040 --> 00:39:35,360
Thanks.

666
00:39:35,400 --> 00:39:36,880
Right.

667
00:39:36,920 --> 00:39:39,840
# Who is knocking
on the door? #

668
00:39:39,880 --> 00:39:41,320
- Thanks a lot.
- # Knocking on the door #

669
00:39:41,360 --> 00:39:43,400
# Knocking on the door #

670
00:39:43,440 --> 00:39:46,040
- # Who is knocking on the door? #
- It's okay, just...

671
00:39:46,080 --> 00:39:48,440
# A way, hey hey. #

672
00:39:48,480 --> 00:39:50,520
Lucy, say hi to the little boy
from the playground.

673
00:39:50,560 --> 00:39:54,280
Hi.

674
00:39:54,320 --> 00:39:56,480
You remember him?

675
00:40:01,520 --> 00:40:03,440
The pool became a ritual.

676
00:40:03,480 --> 00:40:06,080
I was trying to think.
I just didn't know the way.

677
00:40:06,120 --> 00:40:07,840
- Oh oh, okay.
- I'm here, I'm here.

678
00:40:07,880 --> 00:40:09,480
We have the creature
and we have flower.

679
00:40:09,520 --> 00:40:10,680
Right.

680
00:40:10,720 --> 00:40:13,120
Day after day they sat
together in the shade

681
00:40:13,160 --> 00:40:15,080
getting to know
each other.

682
00:40:16,120 --> 00:40:18,840
This needs mustard.

683
00:40:18,880 --> 00:40:21,040
- Mustard?
- Yeah.

684
00:40:21,080 --> 00:40:22,920
Having little choice
in the matter,

685
00:40:22,960 --> 00:40:24,720
Aaron and Lucy formed
a fragile friendship.

686
00:40:30,720 --> 00:40:32,640
Aw, that's perfect.

687
00:40:32,680 --> 00:40:35,480
Sometimes Brad and Sarah
traded offspring.

688
00:40:39,400 --> 00:40:41,440
Mama said, "What Papa
told you was right.

689
00:40:41,480 --> 00:40:44,400
It's not a good idea
to talk to strangers."

690
00:40:44,440 --> 00:40:48,240
It was the most fun
Sarah had had in years.

691
00:41:01,240 --> 00:41:04,160
But there was always
that longing to touch,

692
00:41:04,200 --> 00:41:07,560
to be touched by Brad.

693
00:41:07,600 --> 00:41:11,000
And, as badly as
she wanted this,

694
00:41:11,040 --> 00:41:14,360
she wanted just as badly
to hold on to the innocent public life

695
00:41:14,400 --> 00:41:16,840
they'd made for themselves
out in the open.

696
00:41:16,880 --> 00:41:19,400
So she accepted
the trade--

697
00:41:19,440 --> 00:41:22,400
the melancholy
handshake at 4:00

698
00:41:22,440 --> 00:41:25,400
in exchange for this
little patch of grass,

699
00:41:25,440 --> 00:41:27,960
some sunscreen
and companionship.

700
00:41:28,000 --> 00:41:31,360
One more happy day
at the pool.

701
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:35,600
Okay, no pasta
for dinner, okay?

702
00:41:35,640 --> 00:41:37,920
We eat way too much
pasta around here.

703
00:41:37,960 --> 00:41:39,880
I thought you
liked my pasta.

704
00:41:39,920 --> 00:41:42,400
No, I do.
That's the problem.

705
00:41:42,440 --> 00:41:45,280
Pretty soon I can sell advertising
space on my ass.

706
00:41:46,480 --> 00:41:47,920
No, that's okay.
I've got to go.

707
00:41:47,960 --> 00:41:49,840
I've got
a 9:00 at Taps.

708
00:41:49,880 --> 00:41:51,880
I thought you were
already editing.

709
00:41:51,920 --> 00:41:54,680
Yeah, so did I.
It was just--

710
00:41:54,720 --> 00:41:58,120
there's something in this
family's story that really got to me.

711
00:42:00,680 --> 00:42:02,800
The father was...

712
00:42:02,840 --> 00:42:05,680
K-I-L-L-E-D

713
00:42:05,680 --> 00:42:08,960
in a, um,
mortar attack,

714
00:42:09,000 --> 00:42:11,760
and, um, left behind
a little boy.

715
00:42:14,280 --> 00:42:16,680
I was talking to the mother the other
day on the phone,

716
00:42:16,720 --> 00:42:20,320
and she was saying she didn't know what
she was going to do next Christmas.

717
00:42:20,360 --> 00:42:21,600
Jeez, I bet.

718
00:42:21,640 --> 00:42:24,040
No, it wasn't like that.
It was more...

719
00:42:24,080 --> 00:42:26,960
she was wondering, should she keep
this tradition with her son

720
00:42:26,960 --> 00:42:28,600
that began with
the boy's father.

721
00:42:28,640 --> 00:42:31,320
And she was saying
he had this knack

722
00:42:31,360 --> 00:42:33,960
for requesting
odd Christmas gifts--

723
00:42:34,000 --> 00:42:35,880
scuba gear one year

724
00:42:35,920 --> 00:42:38,440
and rappelling gear
the next.

725
00:42:38,480 --> 00:42:42,280
She said he wasn't
afraid to try anything.

726
00:42:42,320 --> 00:42:44,840
Trying new things
made him feel...

727
00:42:44,880 --> 00:42:47,760
more alive.

728
00:42:49,680 --> 00:42:52,840
I've got to go.
See you later.

729
00:43:01,360 --> 00:43:04,360
Patch one of your best
and then we'll patch both of them.

730
00:43:04,400 --> 00:43:06,240
Okay?

731
00:43:08,880 --> 00:43:11,200
Hey, I got something.

732
00:43:15,400 --> 00:43:17,800
Hot enough for you?

733
00:43:17,840 --> 00:43:20,360
Yeah.

734
00:43:20,400 --> 00:43:23,360
Yeah, it's so humid.

735
00:43:23,400 --> 00:43:26,760
I've got football
practice tonight.

736
00:43:26,800 --> 00:43:28,680
Be like playing
in a sauna.

737
00:43:28,720 --> 00:43:31,920
Watch out for
that Italian guy.

738
00:43:31,920 --> 00:43:34,440
What's his name?

739
00:43:34,480 --> 00:43:35,800
Corrente?

740
00:43:35,840 --> 00:43:38,440
Yeah.

741
00:43:38,480 --> 00:43:40,840
Remember what
happened to your knee last week?

742
00:43:40,880 --> 00:43:43,240
You should be
careful, Brad.

743
00:43:45,920 --> 00:43:47,560
I'll be careful.

744
00:43:47,600 --> 00:43:50,120
Promise?

745
00:43:52,360 --> 00:43:55,960
Yeah.
Yeah, I promise.

746
00:43:58,960 --> 00:44:01,360
Weatherman said
scattered showers.

747
00:44:01,360 --> 00:44:03,280
I don't see
scattered showers.

748
00:44:12,960 --> 00:44:15,720
Mom, could I please
have some money for a snack?

749
00:44:15,760 --> 00:44:18,240
No, sweetheart.
You guys just had a snack. No.

750
00:44:18,280 --> 00:44:19,680
Oh, okay.

751
00:44:19,720 --> 00:44:21,600
All they want is sugar.

752
00:44:21,640 --> 00:44:23,360
Constantly.

753
00:45:38,040 --> 00:45:39,960
Oh, no.

754
00:45:46,800 --> 00:45:49,280
It's him.

755
00:45:50,360 --> 00:45:52,280
Oh, Jesus.

756
00:45:59,480 --> 00:46:01,480
Oh my God,
it's him.

757
00:46:01,520 --> 00:46:04,040
